# Deterministic business rules (product-global)

The LLM must **never** be the only enforcement for critical rules. Implement and validate in backend/domain logic:

- KVKK / privacy consent
- Authorization and tenant isolation
- Clinic activation and agency-connection status where applicable
- Treatment eligibility when defined by product policy
- Pricing-source validation (never invent prices)
- Deterministic recommendation / intake limits when defined by the **current** tenant or agency policy
- Duplicate lead prevention; lead and quote lifecycle
- Appointment status transitions; required intake fields
- Whether side effects are allowed; confirmed side-effect truthfulness (see `40-tools-and-side-effects.mdc`)
- Persisted records and audit state

Agency-specific hard requirements (e.g. FeelinHealthy guest limits, Istanbul side, no-budget) live in scoped rules such as `25-feelinhealthy-agency-rules.mdc` — do **not** apply them to Clinic Portal or unrelated agencies.

When changing rules: update domain modules + tests; do not “fix” only via Prompt Studio copy.
